  "description": "Refactor step M8, class A (docs/plans/codebase-refactor.md §6.5, K1 and K3 in §4.3): internal/api's suite_handlers.go splits along its nine // --- section markers into one file per area and keeps only registerSuiteRoutes. Each section's handlers go with their own helpers, in source order: reference parties to reference_party_handlers.go, the product profile to product_profile_handlers.go, V&V to vv_handlers.go (flowDownCoverage, on the helper-home allowlist already for download_handlers.go, goes with it), requirement quality linting to quality_lint_handlers.go, work items to work_item_handlers.go, guided sessions to guided_handlers.go, the guided copilot chat to guided_copilot_handlers.go (with buildGuidedCopilotPrompt and projectChangeRules, which sit after the public interview section but only the copilot's turns use), internal interviews to interview_handlers.go and the public interview token flow to public_interview_handlers.go. projectExport, which the V&V and quality-lint handlers both load a project's live or baseline export through, goes to project_snapshot.go, which is not an area file. One helper more than one of the new files would use goes to its K3 home instead, so that the helper-home allowlist (M5) gains no entry: getGuidedSessionChecked (the guided session and guided copilot handlers) to authz.go, beside requireWorkerRun, as a load-and-authorize check. launchParent and launchRun, on the allowlist already, stay in agent_run_handlers.go. Preview with: go run ./internal/tools/declmove -n -spec internal/tools/declmove/specs/M8.json",
